From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: File Explorer has tabs

David 2026-10-02: "the file explorer needs to be able to have tabs". As
Windows 11's File Explorer: a strip of tabs above the command bar, each tab
its own folder and its own back and forward; + (or Ctrl+T, or More > New
tab, or a double click on the strip) opens one at Home, a tab's x (or a
middle click, or Ctrl+W) closes it -- the last one, the window; Ctrl+Tab and
Ctrl+Shift+Tab go through them. The strip's window text says what it shows,
for programs that read windows.

Test: test/fetabs-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_TABS_CLOSE_WINDOW); the gates
that click File Explorer at fixed places click below the strip.
---
